---
import StandardPageLayout from "../../layouts/StandardPageLayout.astro";
import PageToc from "../../components/PageToc.astro";
import "../../styles/standards-poster.css";
import "../../styles/extended.css";
import metadata from "../../data/standards/japangaap/asbj32.json";
---

<StandardPageLayout
  code={metadata.code}
  standardType={metadata.framework}
  title={metadata.title}
  description={metadata.summary}
  issued={metadata.issued}
  latestAmendment={metadata.latestAmendment}
  status={metadata.status}
  summary={metadata.summary}
  bannerNotice={metadata.bannerNotice}
>
  <Fragment slot="toc">
    <PageToc
      items={[
        { id: "s1", label: "Conceptual Framework Linkage" },
        { id: "s2", label: "ASBJ's Parallel Numbering Systems — Statements vs Implementation Guidance" },
        { id: "s3", label: "Scope of ASBJ Guidance No. 32" },
        { id: "s4", label: "What This Guidance Provided" },
        { id: "s5", label: "Superseded by the Interim Financial Reporting Package (2025)" },
        { id: "s6", label: "Worked Example — Locating a Cross-Referenced Guidance Number" },
        { id: "s7", label: "Disclosure Requirements" },
        { id: "s8", label: "Critical Judgments" },
        { id: "s9", label: "Relationship to IAS/IFRS" },
        { id: "s10", label: "Statement Mapping" },
        { id: "s11", label: "Related Standards" },
        { id: "s12", label: "Glossary" },
      ]}
    />
  </Fragment>

  <div class="wrap">
    <div class="hub">
      <div class="hub-box">
        <div class="hub-title">ASBJ Guidance No. 32 — Implementation Guidance on Accounting Standard for Semi-annual Financial Reporting</div>
        <div class="hub-sub">Extended reference poster · Japan GAAP (J-GAAP) · A numbering clarification, plus companion Guidance to Statement No. 33 · JPY examples</div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="callout info callout--centered">NUMBERING CLARIFICATION: There is no separately numbered "ASBJ Statement No. 32." Within ASBJ's parallel numbering systems for Statements and Implementation Guidance, "No. 32" in this position corresponds to <strong>ASBJ Guidance No. 32</strong> — the Implementation Guidance issued alongside ASBJ Statement No. 33 (Semi-annual Financial Reporting) in March 2024. This poster explains that companion guidance and the numbering structure itself.</div>

    <div class="toc">
      <a href="#s1">1. Conceptual Framework Linkage</a>
      <a href="#s2">2. ASBJ's Parallel Numbering Systems — Statements vs Implementation Guidance</a>
      <a href="#s3">3. Scope of ASBJ Guidance No. 32</a>
      <a href="#s4">4. What This Guidance Provided</a>
      <a href="#s5">5. Superseded by the Interim Financial Reporting Package (2025)</a>
      <a href="#s6">6. Worked Example — Locating a Cross-Referenced Guidance Number</a>
      <a href="#s7">7. Disclosure Requirements</a>
      <a href="#s8">8. Critical Judgments</a>
      <a href="#s9">9. Relationship to IAS/IFRS</a>
      <a href="#s10">10. Statement Mapping</a>
      <a href="#s11">11. Related Standards</a>
      <a href="#s12">12. Glossary</a>
    </div>

    <div class="section-header" id="s1">
      <span class="num">1</span>
      <h2>Conceptual Framework Linkage</h2>
      <span class="line"></span>
    </div>
    <div class="grid">
      <div class="card ci span2">
        <div class="ctitle ci">Implementation Guidance interprets and operationalises a Statement</div>
        <div class="principle">ASBJ's output is organised into SEVERAL parallel document TYPES — "ACCOUNTING STANDARDS" (ASBJ Statements, the PRIMARY, principle-setting documents), "IMPLEMENTATION GUIDANCE" (detailed, PRACTICAL guidance interpreting and applying a Statement's requirements), "PRACTICAL SOLUTIONS" (narrower, often transitional interpretive guidance), and "TRANSFERRED GUIDANCE" (older interpretive material CARRIED FORWARD from a predecessor body). EACH document type has its OWN, SEPARATE numbering sequence — meaning "No. 32" can refer to DIFFERENT documents depending on WHICH sequence is being referenced.</div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="section-header" id="s2">
      <span class="num">2</span>
      <h2>ASBJ's Parallel Numbering Systems — Statements vs Implementation Guidance</h2>
      <span class="line"></span>
    </div>
    <div class="grid">
      <div class="card cw span2">
        <div class="ctitle cw">Two independently numbered sequences running side by side</div>
        <div class="principle">ACCOUNTING STANDARDS (ASBJ Statements) are numbered 1, 2, 3... independently from IMPLEMENTATION GUIDANCE (ASBJ Guidance), which is ALSO numbered 1, 2, 3... in its OWN, SEPARATE sequence. A Statement and its COMPANION Guidance are OFTEN issued together but do NOT necessarily share the SAME number — for example, ASBJ Statement No. 33 (Semi-annual Financial Reporting) was issued ALONGSIDE ASBJ Guidance No. 32 (its companion Implementation Guidance), NOT "ASBJ Statement No. 32."</div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="section-header" id="s3">
      <span class="num">3</span>
      <h2>Scope of ASBJ Guidance No. 32</h2>
      <span class="line"></span>
    </div>
    <div class="grid">
      <div class="card cd span2">
        <div class="ctitle cd">Practical application guidance for semi-annual reporting</div>
        <div class="text-supporting">
          <div style="font-size:11px;color:var(--color-text-secondary);line-height:1.6;">ASBJ Guidance No. 32 provided DETAILED, PRACTICAL guidance for applying ASBJ Statement No. 33 — the ORIGINAL 2024 Semi-annual Financial Reporting standard (see the companion poster) — addressing SPECIFIC application questions that arise in PREPARING semi-annual (second-quarter) statutory financial statements.</div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="section-header" id="s4">
      <span class="num">4</span>
      <h2>What This Guidance Provided</h2>
      <span class="line"></span>
    </div>
    <div class="grid">
      <div class="card cs span2">
        <div class="ctitle cs">Practical detail supporting the principles set out in Statement No. 33</div>
        <div class="text-supporting">
          <div style="font-size:11px;color:var(--color-text-secondary);line-height:1.6;">Consistent with the GENERAL role of Implementation Guidance across the ASBJ suite, this Guidance SUPPLIED practical, OPERATIONAL detail — illustrative examples, specific application scenarios, and INTERPRETIVE clarifications — supporting COMPANIES in applying Statement No. 33's PRINCIPLES-BASED semi-annual reporting requirements CONSISTENTLY.</div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="section-header" id="s5">
      <span class="num">5</span>
      <h2>Superseded by the Interim Financial Reporting Package (2025)</h2>
      <span class="line"></span>
    </div>
    <div class="grid">
      <div class="card cd span2">
        <div class="ctitle cd">Reworked alongside its parent Statement</div>
        <div class="text-supporting">
          <div style="font-size:11px;color:var(--color-text-secondary);line-height:1.6;">When ASBJ Statement No. 33 was REWORKED into ASBJ Statement No. 37 (Interim Financial Reporting) in October 2025 (see the companion poster), its COMPANION Implementation Guidance was LIKEWISE reworked into <strong>ASBJ Implementation Guidance No. 34</strong> — meaning ASBJ Guidance No. 32's PRACTICAL content has been LARGELY carried forward and updated WITHIN the current Implementation Guidance No. 34, rather than remaining separately in force under its ORIGINAL number.</div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="section-header" id="s6">
      <span class="num">6</span>
      <h2>Worked Example — Locating a Cross-Referenced Guidance Number</h2>
      <span class="line"></span>
    </div>
    <div class="grid">
      <div class="card cw span2">
        <div class="ctitle cw">Resolving a numbering ambiguity in practice</div>
        <div class="worked worked--flush">
          <div class="wk-title">Example: A preparer encountering a reference to "No. 32"</div>
          <div class="wk-body">A preparer researching Japan's semi-annual/interim reporting history encounters a reference to "No. 32" without further qualification.</div>
          <div class="wk-answer">Given the SURROUNDING context (semi-annual reporting, issued alongside Statement No. 33 in March 2024), the preparer can conclude this refers to <strong>ASBJ GUIDANCE No. 32</strong> — the Implementation Guidance companion to Statement No. 33 — NOT a separately numbered Accounting Standard, resolving the AMBIGUITY by recognising ASBJ's TWO parallel numbering sequences.</div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="section-header" id="s7">
      <span class="num">7</span>
      <h2>Disclosure Requirements</h2>
      <span class="line"></span>
    </div>
    <div class="grid">
      <div class="card cd span2">
        <div class="ctitle cd">What this Guidance addressed (now superseded)</div>
        <div class="check-list">
          <span>Practical application scenarios for semi-annual reporting under the original 2024 framework</span>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="section-header" id="s8">
      <span class="num">8</span>
      <h2>Critical Judgments</h2>
      <span class="line"></span>
    </div>
    <div class="grid">
      <div class="card cn span2">
        <div class="ctitle cn">Where judgement matters most</div>
        <div class="two-col">
          <div>
            <div class="elabel">SIGNIFICANT JUDGEMENTS</div>
            <div class="dot-list">
              <span>Correctly identifying which ASBJ numbering sequence a given reference belongs to</span>
            </div>
          </div>
          <div>
            <div class="elabel">SIGNIFICANT ESTIMATES</div>
            <div class="dot-list">
              <span>Not applicable — this is a numbering/reference clarification, not a measurement matter</span>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="section-header" id="s9">
      <span class="num">9</span>
      <h2>Relationship to IAS/IFRS</h2>
      <span class="line"></span>
    </div>
    <div class="grid">
      <div class="card ci span2">
        <div class="ctitle ci">A structural, not substantive, comparison point</div>
        <div class="text-supporting">
          <div style="font-size:11px;color:var(--color-text-secondary);line-height:1.6;">The IASB's OWN standard-numbering convention (IFRS 1, 2, 3... and IAS 1, 2, 3... running as SEPARATE historical sequences) offers a ROUGH parallel to ASBJ's PARALLEL Statement/Guidance numbering — in BOTH systems, a bare NUMBER reference can be AMBIGUOUS without knowing WHICH document type or series it belongs to.</div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="section-header" id="s10">
      <span class="num">10</span>
      <h2>Statement Mapping</h2>
      <span class="line"></span>
    </div>
    <div class="grid">
      <div class="card cs span2">
        <div class="ctitle cs">Not applicable</div>
        <div class="td-table">
          <div class="th cols-16-1-14">
            <span>Event</span>
            <span>Statement(s) affected</span>
            <span>Notes</span>
          </div>
          <div class="tr cols-16-1-14">
            <span>N/A</span>
            <span>N/A</span>
            <span>This is a numbering/reference matter, not a measurement standard</span>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="section-header" id="s11">
      <span class="num">11</span>
      <h2>Related Standards</h2>
      <span class="line"></span>
    </div>
    <div class="grid">
      <div class="card cd span2">
        <div class="ctitle cd">Cross-reference map</div>
        <div class="td-table">
          <div class="th cols-06-24">
            <span>Standard</span>
            <span>Connection</span>
          </div>
          <div class="tr cols-06-24">
            <span>ASBJ Statement No. 33</span>
            <span>The original Semi-annual Financial Reporting standard this Guidance supported</span>
          </div>
          <div class="tr alt cols-06-24">
            <span>ASBJ Statement No. 37 / Guidance No. 34</span>
            <span>The current successor standard and its own companion Implementation Guidance</span>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="section-header" id="s12">
      <span class="num">12</span>
      <h2>Quick-Reference Glossary</h2>
      <span class="line"></span>
    </div>
    <div class="grid">
      <div class="card cn span2">
        <div class="glossary-item">
          <div class="glossary-term">Implementation Guidance (適用指針)</div>
          <div class="glossary-def">Detailed, practical application guidance interpreting an ASBJ Statement, numbered in its own separate sequence from Statements themselves.</div>
        </div>
        <div class="glossary-item glossary-item--last">
          <div class="glossary-term">Companion guidance</div>
          <div class="glossary-def">Implementation Guidance issued alongside a specific Statement to support its practical application, often issued on the same date.</div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="legend">
    <div class="ltitle">Financial statement key (Japan GAAP terminology)</div>
    <div class="lrow">
      <span class="badge bs">BS</span> Balance Sheet (貸借対照表)
      <span class="badge bp">P&amp;L</span> Statement of Income / Profit and Loss Statement (損益計算書)
      <span class="badge bo">Net Assets</span> 純資産の部
      <span class="badge be">SCNA</span> Statement of Changes in Net Assets (株主資本等変動計算書)
      <span class="badge bc">SCF</span> Statement of Cash Flows (キャッシュ・フロー計算書)
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="footer-note">ASBJ Guidance No. 32 — Implementation Guidance on Accounting Standard for Semi-annual Financial Reporting · Extended Reference Poster · Self-contained, no internet connection required</div>
</StandardPageLayout>
